      "html": "† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">בֹּכִים</span></big>  <strong>nome próprio de lugar</strong> perto de Pethel [sic na fonte digital], <span dir=\"rtl\">אל־הַבֹּכִים</span> <a data-ref=\"Judges 2:1\" href=\"/Judges.2.1\">Jz 2.1</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">בֹּכִים</span> versículo <a data-ref=\"Judges 2:5\" href=\"/Judges.2.5\">Jz 2.5</a> (cf. versículo <a data-ref=\"Judges 2:4\" href=\"/Judges.2.4\">Jz 2.4</a>); 𝔊 <a data-ref=\"Judges 2:1\" href=\"/Judges.2.1\">Jz 2.1</a> τὸν Κλαυθμῶνα καὶ ἐμὶ Βαιθηλ; versículo <a data-ref=\"Judges 2:5\" href=\"/Judges.2.5\">Jz 2.5</a> Κλαυθμῶνες isto é, <span dir=\"rtl\">בְּכָיִם</span> (𝔊L Κλαυθμών);—sobre a possível ligação com <span dir=\"rtl\">אַלּוֹן בָּכוּת</span> <a data-ref=\"Genesis 35:8\" href=\"/Genesis.35.8\">Gn 35.8</a> cf. Stu e We<sup>Bleek’s Einl. ed. 4, 183, Comp. Hex. 1889, 215</sup>; mas talvez se leia <span dir=\"rtl\">ביתאל</span> em lugar de <span dir=\"rtl\">בכים</span> no versículo <a data-ref=\"Judges 2:1\" href=\"/Judges.2.1\">Jz 2.1</a>, cf. We Bu<sup>RS 20</sup>.",
